00:15:25.407 --> 00:15:28.037
You wouldn't come here
unless you had a reason.

00:15:31.617 --> 00:15:32.807
You think?

00:15:33.347 --> 00:15:37.407
Even if you might go to the beach
in the winter on your own...

00:15:37.487 --> 00:15:39.387
...would you ever go to an amusement
park alone?

00:15:39.457 --> 00:15:40.617
What does that mean?

00:15:40.857 --> 00:15:44.117
This is the place where
Haseo ceased to be himself.

00:15:45.627 --> 00:15:47.457
Haseo is Haseo.

00:15:47.857 --> 00:15:51.487
I guess he is if you say so even
after his personality has changed.

00:15:53.967 --> 00:15:56.027
Why are you here, Saburou?

00:15:56.107 --> 00:15:57.127
Visiting a grave.

00:15:58.437 --> 00:16:00.637
- What does that mean?
- Exactly what I said.

00:16:03.877 --> 00:16:07.037
I think I may have met Haseo.

00:16:07.117 --> 00:16:08.077
Huh?

00:16:08.147 --> 00:16:12.347
I just couldn't believe
that Shino was a Lost One.

00:16:12.617 --> 00:16:14.317
So I decided to check myself.

00:16:16.487 --> 00:16:19.827
And I'm pretty sure I found her
in a hospital.

00:16:20.127 --> 00:16:22.387
And what about meeting Haseo?

00:16:22.867 --> 00:16:27.167
I heard about a guy around
Haseo's age who visits everyday.

00:16:27.737 --> 00:16:30.257
I passed by him in the hall.

00:16:30.337 --> 00:16:32.237
You think that was Haseo?

00:16:32.807 --> 00:16:33.867
Yeah.

00:16:33.937 --> 00:16:35.067
I see.

00:16:35.507 --> 00:16:40.537
So he thinks of Shino not only
in the game, but in real life too.

00:16:41.717 --> 00:16:44.977
I wish there was something
I could do.

00:16:45.057 --> 00:16:47.887
You came here to think about that?

00:16:48.757 --> 00:16:51.687
I didn't realize you were
so analytical.

00:16:52.827 --> 00:16:55.457
You're not the type of character
that thinks about things.

00:16:55.527 --> 00:16:57.857
It's better just to worry
about one thing.

00:16:59.267 --> 00:17:02.097
Just concentrate
on the most important thing.

00:17:02.467 --> 00:17:06.407
If you mix it all up
you'll never find the answer.

00:17:06.907 --> 00:17:07.967
Right...

00:17:08.247 --> 00:17:11.867
Well, I myself prefer to observe.

00:17:11.947 --> 00:17:14.277
You have all sorts of things
you want to do, right?

00:17:15.787 --> 00:17:19.647
I have an idea of
what I'd like to become.

00:17:20.417 --> 00:17:22.387
Then, I'll keep my eye on you.

00:17:24.227 --> 00:17:26.587
Okay! It's a deal!

00:17:28.267 --> 00:17:30.057
Sorry I'm late.

00:17:31.967 --> 00:17:33.397
Did something happen?

00:17:34.037 --> 00:17:36.297
There's something
we want to show you.

00:17:36.367 --> 00:17:37.397
What is it?

00:17:37.967 --> 00:17:41.377
The reason that we feel Ovan
requires special attention.

00:17:41.777 --> 00:17:44.577
I think showing you might
help you grasp it better.

00:17:53.217 --> 00:17:55.087
Stop it...

00:17:58.327 --> 00:18:00.187
Stop!

00:18:12.737 --> 00:18:14.037
What's happening?

00:18:14.107 --> 00:18:15.537
The data has become enormous!

00:18:15.607 --> 00:18:16.907
I'll handle it!

00:18:18.477 --> 00:18:19.277
Wait.

00:18:24.817 --> 00:18:25.947
What is this?

00:18:28.157 --> 00:18:29.127
Recover it!

00:18:29.187 --> 00:18:30.157
Yes!

00:18:31.557 --> 00:18:32.757
Where did he go?

00:18:32.827 --> 00:18:34.227
What is this?

00:18:34.867 --> 00:18:37.027
What have you done
to that player?

00:18:37.267 --> 00:18:38.997
He has something special.

00:18:39.067 --> 00:18:41.697
No, something utterly foreign.

00:18:42.267 --> 00:18:45.137
Players like him with
unmanageable data...

00:18:45.207 --> 00:18:47.337
...cannot be left alone.

00:18:48.507 --> 00:18:51.067
Someone has to deal with it.

00:18:52.317 --> 00:18:54.777
So, what happened to Ovan?

00:18:56.887 --> 00:18:58.147
He got away.

00:18:58.257 --> 00:18:59.237
How could he?

00:18:59.417 --> 00:19:00.947
Just as you saw here.

00:19:01.017 --> 00:19:02.247
His method is a mystery.

00:19:40.527 --> 00:19:42.517
Are you Mr. Tohta?

00:19:52.037 --> 00:19:55.597
Mr. Tohta, isn't it?

00:19:58.917 --> 00:20:00.377
Yes, it is.

00:20:00.447 --> 00:20:02.817
I was asked to come here.

00:20:02.887 --> 00:20:04.077
If I come...

00:20:04.147 --> 00:20:05.207
I've heard.

00:20:06.617 --> 00:20:07.607
Um...

00:20:07.987 --> 00:20:09.517
I already know.

00:20:09.587 --> 00:20:10.887
Is that right?

00:20:11.527 --> 00:20:13.717
I guess it must be the case.

00:20:14.757 --> 00:20:17.257
Thank you for taking the time.

00:20:17.967 --> 00:20:19.027
Take care.

00:20:26.437 --> 00:20:30.167
I think you can force quit the game
if you need to.

00:20:31.777 --> 00:20:33.437
Oh, yes.

00:20:33.517 --> 00:20:34.707
I'll do that.

00:20:53.337 --> 00:20:58.467
I'm sorry, but I can't return
the feelings you have for me.

00:21:00.377 --> 00:21:02.867
It made me happy, but I can't...

00:21:03.347 --> 00:21:05.307
I can't because...

00:21:06.377 --> 00:21:08.747
...Haseo is trying so hard on his own.

00:21:09.187 --> 00:21:13.447
It's like when Ovan was gone.
Shino had to keep the guild going.

00:21:13.517 --> 00:21:14.677
What do you mean?

00:21:15.487 --> 00:21:18.977
I think I have to
work hard on my own.

00:21:20.527 --> 00:21:24.587
But there are limits to what
one can do by oneself.

00:21:24.667 --> 00:21:27.727
Despite that, I want to face up to it.

00:21:29.537 --> 00:21:30.797
To myself.

00:21:32.877 --> 00:21:34.637
I'm going to try my best!

00:21:34.707 --> 00:21:37.337
And you should try your best
with your new guild, too!

00:21:38.977 --> 00:21:39.947
Bye!

00:21:53.597 --> 00:21:54.687
What is this?

00:21:56.027 --> 00:21:57.157
It can't be...

00:22:05.237 --> 00:22:08.937
So every man for himself, huh?

00:22:30.127 --> 00:22:33.727
Ikiru wa dokuhai kiyu no kurushimi wo
Life is a poisoned cup of needless suffering

00:22:33.797 --> 00:22:37.297
Nomihosu sube wo dare ga sazukeyo
That no one can show me how to drain

00:22:37.567 --> 00:22:40.977
Taiyo ni sumu toiu kenja no washi
A wise eagle is said to live in the sun

00:22:41.037 --> 00:22:45.407
Habataki dake ga kodama suru
The flapping of its wings
is all that echoes

00:22:48.847 --> 00:22:52.377
Kono futatsu no me ni yadotta
In each of these eyes

00:22:52.457 --> 00:22:56.147
Yami to Hikari sono docchi de
Dwell darkness and light

00:22:56.227 --> 00:23:03.457
Boku wa ashita wo mitsumeru
beki nano darou
Through which shall I look to tomorrow?

00:23:03.527 --> 00:23:07.197
Kawaki kitta gareki no machi
A dried out and ruined city

00:23:07.267 --> 00:23:10.967
Ten to sen wo tsunagi awase
Draws the lines between the dots

00:23:11.037 --> 00:23:17.967
Imi nado nai koto bakari afurete iku
Causing meaningless events to overflow

00:23:18.147 --> 00:23:21.807
Honou no gotoki kodoku
Soothing the loneliness

00:23:21.887 --> 00:23:24.907
Idaku karada shizumete wa
That flames up within the body

00:23:24.987 --> 00:23:32.517
Ankyo eto shitatatte iku shizuku
Droplets of water fall towards the culvert

00:23:32.757 --> 00:23:36.317
Kakageru dokuhai kono sei wa michitemo
Even if the poisoned cup is upheld
and filled with this life

00:23:36.427 --> 00:23:40.127
Kogareru shino yume wa nagare tsuku
My dream that yearns for death
drifts into it

00:23:40.337 --> 00:23:43.767
Toride ni kuikomu tsume kokou no washi
The eagle remains aloof;
its talons dig into the fort

00:23:43.837 --> 00:23:47.397
Habataki dake ga maiagaru
Only the flapping of its wings resounds

00:23:47.477 --> 00:23:51.207
Ano soukyu ni takkei ni shite kure tamae
Let me be crucified in the blue sky

00:23:51.277 --> 00:23:54.647
Ten to chi ga musubu basho ni
bokuwa tatsu
I'll stand where heaven and earth meet

00:23:55.947 --> 00:23:57.007
Next Episode
